// NOTE SX_CLOCK_LOOP line 48: The legacy loop polled the clock until the time was up, redrawing its text as fast as it could, at any number of passes; a TeaseScript clock advances only at waits, so a pass after one in which the clock did not advance starts with a wait of a tenth of a second, which also sets how many passes it makes, and the texts the loop says are one message that changes in place.
